# ClipBounce Server Configuration
#
# Quick start: You do NOT need this server to try ClipBounce.
# The extension works in Mock mode immediately after building —
# no server, no API keys, no LM Studio needed.
#
# Only set up this server when you want real AI synthesis via:
#   A) LM Studio / Ollama (free, local) — uncomment AI_PROVIDER=local below
#   B) Anthropic or OpenAI (paid API key) — uncomment ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY

# --- Mock Mode (no server needed) ---
# The extension defaults to Mock mode. Skip this file entirely.
# See README for instructions.

# --- Local LLM Provider (free, OpenAI-compatible, e.g. LM Studio / Ollama) ---
# Uncomment these lines and fill in your model name after starting LM Studio:
# 1. Open LM Studio
# 2. Load a model (e.g. mistral-7b-instruct-v0.2, phi-3-mini, llama-3.2)
# 3. Go to the Server tab and click Start Server
# 4. Copy the EXACT model name from the Server tab
# 5. Set it as LOCAL_LLM_MODEL below
#
# AI_PROVIDER=local
# LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
# LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=           # REQUIRED: set to exact model name loaded in LM Studio
# LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=lm-studio

# --- Paid API Providers ---
# Uncomment and set one key for Anthropic or OpenAI.
# Anthropic takes precedence if both are set.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional: override the default model
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# Server port (default: 8787)
# PORT=8787
